        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yuh-Line Niou, Sheldon Silver\n- Organizations: Democratic Party, New York State Assembly\n- Places: New York City, New York\n- Roles: member of the New York State Assembly, Speaker of the New York State Assembly, lawyer, politician\n- Topics: New York State Assembly 65th district, federal corruption charges\n\nFacts:\n- Sheldon Silver was born on February 13, 1944.\n- Sheldon Silver is a former lawyer and Democratic Party politician from New York City.\n- Sheldon Silver became Speaker of the New York State Assembly in 1994.\n- Sheldon Silver remained Speaker of the New York State Assembly until his arrest on federal corruption charges in 2015.\n- Yuh-Line Niou is a Democratic Party member of the New York State Assembly for New York's 65th district.\n- Yuh-Line Niou holds the New York State Assembly seat for the 65th district that was previously held by Sheldon Silver.",
